WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
Good morning Hank it's Tuesday, May 3rd, 2016

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.160
I gotta go vote, walk with me

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.480
Just an absolutely beautiful day for an election

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.200
Done and done, the best part is you get a sticker

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.540
You'll never guess where I'm going next

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.660
That's right Hank, in a stunning turn of events I find myself in an airport

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.660
*'No Smoking' announcement in Spanish*

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.020
You know my number one complaint about the Indianapolis International Airport...

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.900
...which I truly do believe to be the best airport on Earth

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:19.880
Every 12 minutes...

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.100
I mean, at what point in human history is it just presumed that you can't smoke in an airport

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.740
I think that point is in the past

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.260
On the other hand, I guess if it weren't for that message I would be pretty happy

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.120
just to live he rest of my life in the Indianapolis International Airport

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.420
and maybe that's what they're up to

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.880
maybe they're trying to get me to actually get on a plane.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.820
Today's video, comes to you in 4 very special parts

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.860
Part 1: Voting. I already did that

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.720
Part 2: Hank, today is also my Dad's birthday which I guess means it's your Dad's birthday

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.040
Lots of people don't know this but our Dad basically ran our company until a year ago

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.500
He did like all the payroll and budgeting and spreadsheets that made Crash Course and Sci-Show possible

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.400
He's also a really great Dad and person - Happy Birthday Dad, I love ya

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.040
Why's it so easy to say, 'I love you' to my parents when I can only say it once a year to my brother on, 'Esther Day'?

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.420
Anyway, Part 3: Racing

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.000
So, Hank I'm going to be driving the 'pace car' on May 14th at the 'Angies List' Grand Prix of Indianapolis

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.960
I was very excited about this because I'm a big fan of Indie-Cars

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.000
But then, I, ah went to the track and I tried, I, uh, did my practice

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.840
I thought that being the 'pace car' driver was like a purely ceremonial position

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.500
You know like running with the Olympic Torch or being the Prime Minister of Putin's Russia

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:25.740
But it turns out, no, I have to drive the car, at what is for me, very fast like 110 mph in the straightaways

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.680
Oh and I'm very scared, if you watch it on TV just remember I'm doing my best

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.720
Part 4: Speaking of crashing, God I hope I don't crash, Crash Course

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.760
Hank, here in the United States, millions of high school students are taking their AP Tests right now

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.700
This is always great news for Crash Course: our views sky rocket!

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.540
Anyway, I just wanted to take this opportunity to say to High School students, doing well on tests is great but it is not the point of life

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.240
or the point of education

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:52.320
Tests are a somewhat inefficient way of measuring your understanding of, like, life, the universe and everything

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:58.160
But the point is not to do well on the test, the point is to have a more engaged  and fulfilling life during this

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.300
your one brief flicker of consciousness

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.660
So, Good Luck and study hard, but not just for the test.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.380
Part 5: Did I say there were only gonna be four parts?

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.820
Do I contradict myself? Very well then, I contradict myself.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.580
I am large, I contain multitudes

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.340
Right, Part 5 is my beard

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.200
Hank, as you may have noticed

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.180
I have shaved

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.520
I didn't shave for six consecutive weeks because

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.240
AFC Wimbledon, the 4th tier English soccer team sponsored by Nerdfighteria

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.560
just kept winning!

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.840
And it got to the point where I was pretty desperate to shave but I also

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.960
wanted AFC Wimbledon to make the playoffs

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.640
because if they made the playoffs, they'd have a 25% chance of becoming a 3rd tier English soccer team

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.760
And it's always been my dream to sponsor a 3rd tier English soccer team

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.240
And then, Hank, the most amazing thing happened!

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.180
First, AFC Wimbledon lost a game, allowing me to shave, and then

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:42.320
another team didn't win a game, allowing AFC Wimbledon to make the playoffs anyway!

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.520
So good luck to AFC Wimbledon

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.580
If they make it to the finals, Hank, I am going to Wimbly stadium to watch the game

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.500
Also Vice Sports made a great documentary about the team and my relationship with them

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.160
So check that out

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.600
Part 6: Last part I promise.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.820
Vidcon! Nerdfighters if you want to participate in the si-

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.980
*No smoking announcement in Spanish*

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.360
I know I can't fumar!

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.040
If you want to participate in the signings and meet-and-greets you have to register by May 13th

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.100
so fair warning

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.120
Alright the no smoking messages have gotten annoying enough that I'm going to get on the plane.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.240
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

